# Live Trading

Full reference: `docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`

## Config merge

- `resolve_live_startup()` in `provider_utils.py` merges `config/live.yaml` with API overrides
- Flattened `risk:` block goes into engine config (kill switch, exposure limits, `regime_overlay`)
- Empty `POST /api/live/start` body uses YAML defaults

## Auto-start (systemd)

- `FIRM_AUTO_START_LIVE=1` → `bootstrap_live_from_yaml()` in `live.py`
- Runs via `asyncio.to_thread()` in `app.py` lifespan — not on uvicorn's event loop
- Failures are logged; API stays up for manual start

## Providers

- `build_live_providers("ibkr_paper")` → IBKR prices/sentiment + FMP → … fundamentals fallback chain
- Fundamentals cache refreshes in-app: daily APScheduler job + boot when stale (`fundamentals_refresh_hour` in `live.yaml`); live cycles are cache-only
- Data provider uses `client_id=2`; broker uses `IBKR_CLIENT_ID`

## Approval modes

Only `full_auto` and `semi_auto` are valid. Anything else queues all orders.

## Live config round-trip (behavioural knobs)

- `GET`/`PUT /api/live/config` and `POST /api/live/start` round-trip `news_guard`, `signal_combination`, `allocation_method`, `kelly_fraction` (alongside strategies/risk/universe)
- Apply on a running engine via setters: `update_news_guard()` (sets `_news_guard_*` attrs), `update_signal_combination()` / `update_allocation()` (merge `_config` + **rebuild orchestrator**)
- Any `update_*` that rebuilds the orchestrator must go through `LiveTradingEngine._rebuild_orchestrator()` — it preserves per-sleeve state (see below) across the rebuild; don't call `build_orchestrator()` directly from an update method
- YAML in `config/live.yaml`; `resolve_live_startup()` seeds `engine_config`; explicit request fields override
- UI: `frontend/src/pages/LiveConfig.tsx`

## Capital sleeves (`capital_allocation_mode`)

- `blended` (default) = today's single shared `PortfolioState`; `sleeved` = one independent `PortfolioState` + `TraderAgent` per strategy, netted into one real order set only at the final `ExecutionAgent` pass (its own, smaller `real_rebalance_band_pct` — the blended-mode band is far too wide once capital splits N ways)
- Start-time only, like `broker` — not hot-swappable via `PUT /api/live/config`, requires a restart
- `capital_allocation_mode`/`strategy_capital_weights`/`real_rebalance_band_pct` must be in **both** `StartRequest` (manual API) and `resolve_live_startup()`'s YAML allowlist (`provider_utils.py`) — these are two separate wiring paths, easy to update only one
- Cutover on a live engine with real positions: seed sleeves once via `POST /api/live/sleeves/seed` (best-effort split from broker positions + existing attribution; refuses a second call)
- Full design/history: `docs/capital_sleeves_plan.md`

## Ops

- Status: `GET /api/live/status` — watch `cycle_running_seconds` for stuck cycles
- Two instances, two units: `:8000` IBKR (`deploy/ai-trading.service`, `config/live.yaml`, blended) and `:8001` Alpaca (`config/live_alpaca.yaml`, sleeved)

## Editing code while services run (2026-09-28)
- Both `firm-api` services import from this checkout. Never modify tracked `src/` while `ai-trading` / `ai-trading-alpaca` is active: modules are lazily imported mid-run, so an uncommitted edit can produce a mixed-version process (an ImportError failed IBKR cycle 109). Use a `git worktree`, or stop the services first.
- `signal_combination.estimator` is `legacy` (default, live) or `robust` (off, see `docs/optimal_combination_fix_2026_09.md`). The Live Config / New Backtest pages preserve all `signal_combination` keys on save.
- `rebalance_fraction` is per *trading day*, not per cycle (2026-09-29): `ExecutionAgent._day_anchor` anchors each (book, symbol) at its first order of the day. Any new per-period knob must be cadence-aware the same way, because live runs ~7 cycles per day and the backtest runs 1.

## Allocation mode (2026-09-30, opt-in, not live until owner sign-off)
- `strategy_mode: allocation` bypasses the strategy/analyst/PM/risk pipeline; `src/firm/allocation/` sleeves → targets of current NAV → orders via `_execute_orders`. Default `pipeline` unchanged (IBKR).
- Safety invariants (tested in `tests/test_allocation_review_fixes.py`): market-open only, no planning while orders are open, marks checked vs last close, leverage backstop at last-close prices, `submitting` persisted before routing, `full_auto` required, `cash_buffer`.
- Deploy only via `docs/allocation_deploy_runbook.md` with owner sign-off on the exact `config/live_alpaca.yaml` diff.

